>
  <p>Nuvellum Studio is a separate commercial service offered by Nuvellum’s publisher. It applies practical experience from operating an independent digital publication to the work behind other publications: editorial workflows, publishing infrastructure and distribution. It is not a paid route to coverage in Nuvellum.</p>

  <h2>Publication workflow audit — $125</h2>
  <p>A fixed-price starting point for an independent publisher, newsletter or small media team. We review <strong>one live publication and one existing publishing workflow</strong>, then deliver a concise diagnostic, a prioritized list of risks and opportunities, and a suggested next-step plan. Covers publishing reliability, source and approval handoffs, essential discovery metadata and distribution touchpoints. Includes one 20-minute remote handoff. Typical delivery is within five business days once access and materials are supplied.</p>
  <p><a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Studio%20%E2%80%94%20Publication%20workflow%20audit%20%24125">Enquire about the $125 audit →</a></p>

  <h2>Distribution and SEO setup — $240</h2>
  <p>For a publication with a working site but inconsistent discoverability. Includes a site and metadata review, RSS and sitemap checks, social-preview validation, and implementation of <strong>up to three agreed, bounded fixes</strong> where access permits. A documented handover is included. This is an infrastructure service, not a promise of search rankings, social reach or advertising approval.</p>
  <p><a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Studio%20%E2%80%94%20Distribution%20and%20SEO%20setup%20%24240">Enquire about the $240 setup →</a></p>

  <h2>Newsroom automation sprint — from $450</h2>
  <p>Design, implement and test one scoped editorial or distribution workflow using the client’s existing tools. The handover includes operating instructions, a safe failure path and basic acceptance tests. The final quote depends on integrations, hosting, data access and third-party limits. External software, API, advertising and hosting charges remain the client’s responsibility.</p>
  <p><a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Studio%20%E2%80%94%20Automation%20sprint">Discuss an automation sprint →</a></p>

  <h2>How an engagement works</h2>
  <p>Send a short description of the publication, the current process and the problem to solve. We confirm the deliverables, access requirements, schedule and fixed price in writing before paid work begins. We do not request passwords by email; access is provided through appropriate account permissions. Scope changes require a fresh agreement.</p>

  <h2>Editorial separation</h2>
  <p>These commercial services do not purchase editorial coverage, favorable treatment, story placement or influence over <a href="/standards">Nuvellum’s reporting standards</a>. Sponsored placements, if offered separately, must be labeled and are handled through the <a href="/advertise">advertising desk</a>. Client materials are used only for the contracted service and are not incorporated into journalism without an independent editorial basis.</p>

  <h2>Enquiries</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Nuvellum%20Studio%20enquiry">sam@nuvellum.news</a> with your site URL, the issue and the timeline. USD prices are introductory project rates, not subscriptions; availability and final scope are confirmed individually.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
